# Allowlist, not a denylist: Claude Code writes new runtime state files into
# this directory over time (credentials, session transcripts, shell snapshots,
# caches). A denylist silently fails open the first time a new one appears —
# which is how .credentials.json ended up stageable. Ignore everything and
# opt in the config we actually want to sync across machines.

*

!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json

# skills/ stays ignored: it is *generated*, not authored. ../setup.sh compiles
# it from ../../core (model-agnostic steps + scripts) and ../../adapters/claude
# (frontmatter), and its last step deletes this directory outright. Committing
# the output put a stale SKILL.md and a symlink to an absolute $HOME path into
# a public repo. Edit core/ and adapters/; re-run setup.sh to regenerate.
